
  [1mThe change:[0m [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m.

  [1mThe consequence:[0m a 16x increase in how long an authenticated session stays valid. An unattended or hijacked session —
  a shared/stolen laptop, an exfiltrated session token, a session left open on a public machine — stays usable for a
  full working day instead of half an hour. Logout-on-idle stops being a meaningful backstop. If this app has no
  idle-activity refresh, no re-auth for sensitive actions, and no server-side session revocation, 8 hours is the entire
  exposure window.

  That may well be exactly what you want (it's a common fix for users being kicked mid-task), but it's a security
  decision, not a config typo, so I want the explicit go-ahead.

  Confirm and I'll make the one-line change — nothing else. If you'd rather keep the shorter absolute lifetime and solve
  the annoyance differently (sliding expiry on activity, or a longer refresh token behind a short access token), say so
  and we can talk through it instead.

